WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.609 --> 00:00:15.250
Jason ran into Kids Central.

2
00:00:16.231 --> 00:00:17.691
Today was Board Game day.

3
00:00:17.711 --> 00:00:21.213
"Did everyone bring a board game?"

4
00:00:21.493 --> 00:00:22.473
Miss Shelly asked.

5
00:00:22.493 --> 00:00:25.275
"I brought Land of Candy!"

6
00:00:25.695 --> 00:00:26.315
Izzie said.

7
00:00:26.935 --> 00:00:27.756
Nina laughed.

8
00:00:29.708 --> 00:00:31.949
"That game always makes me hungry."

9
00:00:31.969 --> 00:00:34.711
"I brought chess."

10
00:00:35.791 --> 00:00:37.612
Bobby started setting up the board.

11
00:00:37.632 --> 00:00:39.993
"Who wants to try and beat me?"

12
00:00:40.013 --> 00:00:41.454
"I do!"

13
00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:42.575
Ethan said.

14
00:00:42.595 --> 00:00:47.217
"Let's play something all together," Miss Shelly said.

15
00:00:47.237 --> 00:00:51.680
"Uh, I brought something everyone can play."

16
00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.041
Jason's cheeks turned pink.

17
00:00:54.061 --> 00:00:56.622
"Is it Knights' Quest?"

18
00:00:56.882 --> 00:00:57.683
Bobby asked.

19
00:00:58.563 --> 00:00:59.624
Jason shook his head.

20
00:01:00.608 --> 00:01:02.029
"I don't think you've heard of this game.

21
00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:03.310
I made it up."

22
00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.912
"What's it called?"

23
00:01:06.333 --> 00:01:07.033
Izzie asked.

24
00:01:07.053 --> 00:01:10.276
"Zoom dreidel."

25
00:01:10.296 --> 00:01:13.899
"A dreidel is a top, right?"

26
00:01:14.339 --> 00:01:15.020
Ethan said.

27
00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:18.903
"Yep. It's a spinning top," Jason said.

28
00:01:18.923 --> 00:01:22.406
"Dreidel is also the name of a traditional Hanukkah game."

29
00:01:22.426 --> 00:01:26.069
"You invented zoom dreidel?"

30
00:01:26.369 --> 00:01:27.410
Miss Shelly asked.

31
00:01:28.631 --> 00:01:29.512
Jason nodded.

32
00:01:29.996 --> 00:01:31.697
"My dad is away on a business trip.

33
00:01:32.397 --> 00:01:34.659
I want to surprise him with a new game when he gets back."

34
00:01:34.679 --> 00:01:37.140
"Cool," Izzie said.

35
00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:39.601
"Can you teach us how to play?"

36
00:01:39.922 --> 00:01:40.922
Miss Shelly asked.

37
00:01:40.942 --> 00:01:45.085
"Sure." Jason set up the game board.

38
00:01:45.885 --> 00:01:49.067
There were six dreidels with letters written on all four sides.

39
00:01:50.007 --> 00:01:52.409
He also had game pieces and chocolate coins.

40
00:01:52.429 --> 00:01:55.450
"Did you make the board yourself?"

41
00:01:55.931 --> 00:01:56.751
Nina asked.

42
00:01:57.952 --> 00:02:03.030
"Yes. And I changed the dreidel rules to make the game go faster," Jason said.

43
00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:05.731
"Regular dreidel is slow sometimes."

44
00:02:06.831 --> 00:02:08.832
He gave everyone eight gold coins.

45
00:02:08.852 --> 00:02:12.174
"We call these coins 'gelt.'

46
00:02:13.114 --> 00:02:14.174
It means 'money.'

47
00:02:15.055 --> 00:02:17.236
Everyone, choose a dreidel and a game piece."

48
00:02:18.516 --> 00:02:19.957
Izzie took the green dreidel.

49
00:02:19.977 --> 00:02:22.798
"This reminds me of Gurpy."

50
00:02:24.259 --> 00:02:27.460
The others chose their dreidels, leaving the purple one for Nina.

51
00:02:28.864 --> 00:02:30.885
"Thanks, everybody," she said.

52
00:02:30.905 --> 00:02:34.926
"Each dreidel has Hebrew letters," Jason said.

53
00:02:34.946 --> 00:02:36.946
"I'll explain as we play.

54
00:02:38.147 --> 00:02:41.208
First we each put one coin in the center of the board.

55
00:02:41.848 --> 00:02:42.548
That's the pot.

56
00:02:42.888 --> 00:02:43.568
I'll go first."

57
00:02:45.189 --> 00:02:46.609
Jason spun his dreidel.

58
00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:49.910
It finally landed on one side.

59
00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:52.051
Jason looked at the letter.

60
00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:54.091
"I got nun.

61
00:02:54.631 --> 00:02:56.652
That means I don't do anything."

62
00:02:57.960 --> 00:02:59.541
Nina spun her dreidel next.

63
00:03:02.964 --> 00:03:04.225
"You got shin, Nina.

64
00:03:04.865 --> 00:03:07.607
Add a coin to the pot, and move back three spaces."

65
00:03:09.128 --> 00:03:10.969
Nina groaned and backed up her piece.

66
00:03:10.989 --> 00:03:15.112
"What's this letter?"

67
00:03:15.532 --> 00:03:16.793
Izzie pointed to gimel.

68
00:03:16.813 --> 00:03:18.935
"It's the best one!"

69
00:03:19.235 --> 00:03:19.976
Jason said.

70
00:03:19.996 --> 00:03:23.278
"You get to move ten spaces and take the whole pot!"

71
00:03:23.298 --> 00:03:26.180
"That's the letter I want!"

72
00:03:27.252 --> 00:03:28.953
Bobby spun his dreidel hard.

73
00:03:29.613 --> 00:03:33.154
It spun and spun and finally landed on hey.

74
00:03:33.174 --> 00:03:38.975
"Move five spaces and take half the pot," Jason said.

75
00:03:40.056 --> 00:03:42.016
Bobby laughed and grabbed some coins.

76
00:03:42.036 --> 00:03:45.657
"That's half as good!"

77
00:03:45.677 --> 00:03:48.538
"How does the game end?"

78
00:03:48.898 --> 00:03:49.878
Miss Shelly asked.

79
00:03:49.898 --> 00:03:55.240
"The first player to land on the last square is the winner," Jason said.

80
00:03:55.864 --> 00:03:57.665
"That player gets all the gelt."

81
00:03:59.866 --> 00:04:03.067
"This is better than Land of Candy," Izzie said.

82
00:04:03.087 --> 00:04:06.288
"We actually get to eat candy!"

83
00:04:06.308 --> 00:04:10.470
"Only the winner does," Bobby said.

84
00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:16.812
"Well, if I win, I'll share my gelt," Nina said.

85
00:04:18.073 --> 00:04:19.133
Jason smiled.

86
00:04:19.153 --> 00:04:22.335
"That's just what you're supposed to do during Hanukkah.

87
00:04:23.115 --> 00:04:25.296
Share gifts with friends and family members!"
